[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_6cn5t")
entry_name = "Input() "
description = "In Python we have what we call the user input and to get and store that user input we would need to declare an input function for that.

Here is some sample codes using the user input.

first_name = input(\"Enter your first name: \")
output: Enter your first name: 

We first declare a variable called first_name to hold the user input of their first name.
Note that in Python all user inputs are going to be saved as strings, even if the user inputs numbers Python will read it as a string.

we used the input(\"\") to ask for their name, that's basically how you would use the user input in Python.

The output will be \"Enter your first name: \" it's like printing right? but here the user can now provide inputs."
keyword = "Input(\"\")"
language = "python"
category = "Easy"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://c8mblthys4abt"
